{"type":"text","timestamp":1790366162712,"sessionID":"ses_f25e18997ffe3PbBK4AUjZeTgZ","part":{"id":"prt_0da239f10001Iv83sd0bOcC1Nm","messageID":"msg_0da207d08001Nkq82U4b9tITRk","sessionID":"ses_f25e18997ffe3PbBK4AUjZeTgZ","type":"text","text":"The boss sheet uses a 10×10 grid: idle is row 0 frame 0, walk is row 1 frames 0–7, and hurt is row 7 frames 0–1. I’ll preserve every non-empty frame in those rows and add a melee punch row for the enemy so its emitter can damage the player.","time":{"start":1790366162704,"end":1790366162706},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0be74aff0fb51d6e016ab6d1b281f081979734f3a952b5659f","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790366162727,"sessionID":"ses_f25e18997ffe3PbBK4AUjZeTgZ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_vbVfDVQtJeeL6LFlKrABpxmT","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/scenes/characters/character.gd\n@@\n @export var damage : int\n @export var health : int\n @export var speed : float\n+@export var knockback_speed : float = 40.0\n \n @onready var animation_player := $AnimationPlayer\n @onready var character_sprite := $CharacterSprite\n @onready var damage_emitter := $DamageEmitter\n+@onready var damage_receiver := $DamageReceiver\n \n-enum State {IDLE, WALK, ATTACK}\n+enum State {IDLE, WALK, ATTACK, HURT}\n \n var state := State.IDLE\n+var remove_after_hurt := false\n \n func _ready() -> void:\n-\tdamage_emitter.area_entered.connect(on_emit_damage.bind())\n+\tdamage_emitter.area_entered.connect(on_emit_damage)\n+\tdamage_receiver.damage_received.connect(on_receive_damage)\n \n func _process(_delta: float) -> void:\n@@\n func handle_movement() -> void:\n+\tif state == State.HURT:\n+\t\treturn\n \tif can_move():\n@@\n func handle_input() -> void:\n+\tif state == State.HURT:\n+\t\treturn\n \tvar direction := Input.get_vector(\"ui_left\", \"ui_right\", \"ui_up\", \"ui_down\")\n@@\n \tif state == State.IDLE:\n-\t\tanimation_player.play(\"idle\")\n+\t\tplay_animation(\"idle\")\n \telif state == State.WALK:\n-\t\tanimation_player.play(\"walk\")\n+\t\tplay_animation(\"walk\")\n \telif state == State.ATTACK:\n-\t\tanimation_player.play(\"punch\")\n+\t\tplay_animation(\"punch\")\n+\telif state == State.HURT:\n+\t\tplay_animation(\"hurt\")\n@@\n func can_attack() -> bool:\n \treturn state == State.IDLE or state == State.ATTACK\n \n func on_action_complete() -> void:\n-\tstate = State.IDLE\n+\tif state == State.ATTACK:\n+\t\tstate = State.IDLE\n+\n+func on_hurt_complete() -> void:\n+\tif state != State.HURT:\n+\t\treturn\n+\tif remove_after_hurt:\n+\t\tqueue_free()\n+\telse:\n+